 "editorial": {
  "cups": {
   "2025.l.40764.t.9": "Built a champion out of everyone else's cuts.",
   "2025.l.40764.t.1": "Lost the final to two players he dropped.",
   "2025.l.40764.t.10": "Stole bronze by 19 points. Vishal will take it.",
   "2025.l.40764.t.6": "Parked in 8th for five straight weeks, then lost bronze by 19 points."
  },
  "bubble": {
   "headline": "Parth Squeaks In, Two Contenders Fall Off the Ledge",
   "sub": "Six playoff spots, decided on the last day of the regular season.",
   "cards": [
    {
     "team": "2025.l.40764.t.6",
     "tag": "Snuck in",
     "body": "Outside the line for 16 of 19 weeks, including five straight parked in 8th. Final week: a 9-2 beating of last-place Acinonyx while MONSTARS face-planted. In by a hair, then hung a 10-1 on the 3 seed in the quarters."
    },
    {
     "team": "2025.l.40764.t.12",
     "tag": "Back from the dead",
     "body": "Dead last in Week 2. Finished as the 4 seed after closing the regular season with a 9-2 demolition of Gopher Gold. Nobody saw it coming, least of all Gopher Gold."
    },
    {
     "team": "2025.l.40764.t.5",
     "tag": "Crashed out",
     "body": "Held a playoff spot for 12 weeks and walked into the final week sitting 6th. Lost 2-9 to the 9th-place Nova Knicks. Season over by Sunday."
    },
    {
     "team": "2025.l.40764.t.4",
     "tag": "Crashed out",
     "body": "Was No. 1 in Week 4 and spent 15 weeks inside the line. Then slid from 4th to 8th over the final five weeks, capped by a 2-9 beatdown. A full collapse, start to finish."
    }
   ]
  },
  "spicy": {
   "22-1-9": {
    "headline": "John J Gets Killed by His Own Cuts",
    "body": [
     "John J had the volume. Luka dropped 116, Kawhi 103, and theInfamous outscored Thug Life by 79 points and won the threes. For a minute, the trophy looked like it had his name on it.",
     "Then the receipts came in. Nickeil Alexander-Walker, drafted by John J for $1 and cut, put up 94 points, 13 threes and 7 steals for Arnav. Josh Hart, another John J cast-off, added 21 rebounds and 7 steals. Joki\u0107 piled on 68 rebounds and 56 assists, and Thug Life swept steals, assists and turnovers.",
     "The dagger: defensive rebounds, theInfamous's best category all season, went to Thug Life by four. Beaten at your own game by players you threw away."
    ]
   },
   "22-6-10": {
    "headline": "Parth Loses Bronze by Nineteen Points",
    "body": [
     "Third place, nothing on the line but pride, and Parth still found a way to make it hurt. LeParth James won blocks by 19, turnovers by 25 and offensive boards by 17. Brunson poured in 90. Wembanyama swatted 13.",
     "It came down to points, and Parth lost them by 19. Vishal's pickups did the damage: Bennedict Mathurin and Olivier-Maxence Prosper threw in 68 apiece.",
     "Steals, normally Parth's best category, went the other way. So did assists. Bronze slipped to Vishal, and Parth takes home the Tin Cup."
    ]
   }
  }
 },
